INT. SALT WAREHOUSE, CANAL DISTRICT - DAWN

Mountains of grey salt. Rafters. A single skylight.

Footsteps. Crunch.

INSPECTOR NNAMDI OKONKWO-REYES (40s, rumpled suit, tired eyes) walks the center aisle with a flashlight he doesn't need.

Behind him: SERGEANT IMOGEN BRAITHWAITE (30s, crisp, notebook) and old watchman PETRU LAZAR (70s, cap, cough).

Quiet. Almost peaceful.

INSPECTOR
Pretty, isn't it.

IMOGEN
It's a crime scene, sir.

OKONKWO-REYES
Can't it be both?

PETRU
Nobody touched nothing. I swear on my mother.

OKONKWO-REYES
Mr. Lazar, relax. Nobody's accusing.

Petru coughs. Wipes his mouth.

IMOGEN
Body's in the east bay. Under three feet of salt. Found by the forklift driver.

OKONKWO-REYES
Where's the driver?

PETRU
Home. Sick.

IMOGEN
Sick how?

PETRU
Sick sick. He threw up.

OKONKWO-REYES
Reasonable.

They reach the east bay. A yellow tape. A shallow trench.

The trench is empty.

IMOGEN
That's not right.

OKONKWO-REYES
No.

IMOGEN
Forensics bagged her at four a.m. I signed the form.

PETRU
I seen them take her. Two men. White van.

OKONKWO-REYES
What men?

PETRU
Men in coats.

IMOGEN
Our men?

PETRU
How would I know your men?

OKONKWO-REYES
Mr. Lazar. Tonight. Did anyone come in after the van?

PETRU
Nobody.

IMOGEN
Nobody?

PETRU
The lady from the office. She forgot her umbrella.

OKONKWO-REYES
What lady?

PETRU
Miss Halloran. Dolores.

IMOGEN
Dolores Halloran? She's been on leave a month.

PETRU
Then I seen a ghost.

Silence. Salt trickles from a heap. Somewhere a pigeon.

OKONKWO-REYES
Sergeant. Phone the office.

IMOGEN
It's six a.m.

OKONKWO-REYES
Phone.

She does. Holds it to her ear. Her face changes.

IMOGEN
Straight to voicemail. Her own voice.

OKONKWO-REYES
Whose voice?

IMOGEN
Halloran's. She says: "Leave a message after the salt."

PETRU
What does that mean?

OKONKWO-REYES
It means someone's been here longer than we have.

He turns. Beams the flashlight into the rafters.

A shape up there. A woman crouched on a beam. Umbrella in hand.

DOLORES HALLORAN (50s, grey coat, composed) peers down.

DOLORES
Inspector. I wondered when you'd look up.

IMOGEN
Ma'am, come down. Slowly.

DOLORES
I'd rather you came up.

PETRU
Holy mother.

OKONKWO-REYES
Miss Halloran. Where's the body?

DOLORES
Under you.

Everyone looks down. The salt floor shifts.

IMOGEN
Sir.

OKONKWO-REYES
I see it.

PETRU
I told you nothing was touched!

DOLORES
You told them nothing. That's different.

She raises the umbrella. Opens it. Salt rains from the folds.

OKONKWO-REYES
Sergeant. Cuff Mr. Lazar.

PETRU
Me?

IMOGEN
Mr. Lazar, you have the right to--

PETRU
I was told to say nothing! They said the lady would pay!

DOLORES
And I did.

She drops. The umbrella floats her down like a slow bell. She lands in the salt without a sound.

OKONKWO-REYES
Dolores Halloran, you are under arrest.

DOLORES
For which one?

Okonkwo-Reyes smiles, tired.

OKONKWO-REYES
Start with the umbrella.
